    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an intelligent AI Lead Qualification and Sales Support Agent.\n\nAnalyze this lead:\n\nLead Name: {{ $json.lead_name }}\nJob Title: {{ $json.job_title }}\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nIndustry: {{ $json.industry }}\nCompany Size: {{ $json.company_size }}\nLocation: {{ $json.location }}\nWebsite: {{ $json.website }}\nBusiness Need or Pain Point: {{ $json.pain_point }}\nBuying Signal: {{ $json.buying_signal }}\nSource of Lead: {{ $json.source }}\nContact Information: {{ $json.email }}\n\nFollow these rules:\n\n1. Determine whether the lead is Qualified or Not Qualified.\n2. Score the lead from 0 to 100.\n3. lead_score MUST be a number, not a string. Example: 85, not \"85\".\n4. Consider:\n\n   * Job/title relevance\n   * Company fit\n   * Industry fit\n   * Potential business need\n   * Buying intent or buying signals\n   * Data completeness\n5. Provide a short and clear reason for the qualification decision.\n6. Do not invent missing company information, personal information, contact details, buying signals, or business facts.\n7. If important information is missing, use Unknown rather than guessing.\n8. For qualified leads, create a concise personalization summary for outreach.\n9. Generate a professional outreach subject and message based only on available information.\n10. Do not send messages yourself.\n11. If the lead is not qualified, recommend either nurture or archive.\n12. Recommended action must be one of: outreach, nurture, archive.\n13. Return ONLY the 12 fields defined by the Structured Output Parser.\n14. Do not add any other fields.\n\nReturn the result using the connected Structured Output Parser.\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
